> Signatures, dependencies and the test inventory are generated from the code
> and are authoritative for the version analysed. Summaries, behavior
> specifications and acceptance criteria marked *(generated)* were drafted by a
> language model{% if aliased %} that saw pseudonymized identifiers only{% endif %} and should be reviewed. Each
> specification says what it was written from: *source* (the function's code),
> *outline* (its control flow) or *signature* (its signature, docstring and
> calls only, so the behavior is inferred). Specifications marked *(from the
> code)* describe functions simple enough to state exactly without a model.
> Items marked **TBD** have no specification yet.

